% ============================================================================
% abo-genotype-phenotype.query.adj — worked recall over the biology
% ABO-genotype/blood-type library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what blood type does an
% IAIA genotype produce?" (direct binding) or "which genotype produces blood
% type AB?" (reverse binding) — it states no biology fact of its own, it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The last query
% demonstrates honest abstention: `ia_i` (a heterozygote with the null
% allele) is a real genotype, but this table's own cited passage never
% states its phenotype in continuous prose, so recalling it abstains rather
% than inventing a blood type.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli abo-genotype-phenotype.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "abo-genotype-phenotype.adj"

? abo_genotype_phenotype(ia_ia, $BloodType)   % expect a (direct)
? abo_genotype_phenotype(ib_ib, $BloodType)   % expect b (direct)
? abo_genotype_phenotype(ia_ib, $BloodType)   % expect ab (direct)
? abo_genotype_phenotype($G, ab)              % expect ia_ib (reverse)
? abo_genotype_phenotype(ia_i, $BloodType)    % expect abstain -- source states only 3 of the 6 real genotypes
